  "solution": "Logic followed here:\n\n**2nd Number = (1st number × 2 + 3rd number × 3)**\n\nWe have\n\n(39, 117, 13)\n\n⇒ (39 × 2 + 13 × 3) = 78 + 39 = 117 \n\n(48, 99, 1)\n\n⇒ (48 × 2 + 1 × 3) = 96 + 3 = 99\n\n**Check Options:**\n\nOption (1): (8, 42, 10)\n\n⇒ (8 × 2 + 10 × 3) = 16 + 30 = 46 (false)\n\nOption (2): (35, 138, 24)\n\n⇒ (35 × 2 + 24 × 3) = 70 + 72 = 142 (false)\n\nOption (3): (19, 106, 24)\n\n⇒ (19 × 2 + 24 × 3) = 38 + 72 = 110 (false)\n\n**Option (4): (27, 117, 21)**\n\n⇒ (27 × 2 + 21 × 3) = 54 + 63 = 117 **(true)**\n\nHence, the correct answer is **Option 4.**",
